 "description": "Bianconi2012 - EGFR and IGF1R pathway in lung cancer\nBioModels BIOMD0000000427 (curated). SBML file: BIOMD0000000427_url.xml.\nSimulation: 0 to 3000 time units (SED-ML: BIOMD0000000427_url.sedml (auto-generated placeholder); duration chosen from the dynamics: settled), sampling 3.\nRun switches: -ig:mass -INT:1 -obeymaxint\nVerification against libRoadRunner (SBML reference): PASS, max |difference| = 4.46e-06 of species peak (worst: ERK_active)\nSBML time units are used unchanged as Kintecus seconds.\nConversion notes:\n  [info] SOS_conformational_activation: rate is not proportional to its reactants; divided form used with 1/(c+1e-30) so an empty species is not consumed\n  [info] kRas_Activation: rate is not proportional to its reactants; divided form used with 1/(c+1e-30) so an empty species is not consumed\n  [info] ERK_activationBy_Mek: rate is not proportional to its reactants; divided form used with 1/(c+1e-30) so an empty species is not consumed\n  [info] SOS_deactivationBy_P90: rate is not proportional to its reactants; divided form used with 1/(c+1e-30) so an empty species is not consumed\n  [info] SOS_activationBy_IGF: rate is not proportional to its reactants; divided form used with 1/(c+1e-30) so an empty species is not consumed\n  [info] PI3KCA_activationBy_IGF1R: rate is not proportional to its reactants; divided form used with 1/(c+1e-30) so an empty species is not consumed\n  [info] PI3KCA_activationBy_EGF: rate is not proportional to its reactants; divided form used with 1/(c+1e-30) so an empty species is not consumed\n  [info] Akt_activationBy_PI3KCA: rate is not proportional to its reactants; divided form used with 1/(c+1e-30) so an empty species is not consumed\n  [info] ERK_deactivationBy_PP2A: rate order differs from the stoichiometry; consumed on separate line(s) - \n  [info] PI3KCA_activationBy_kRas: rate is not proportional to its reactants; divided form used with 1/(c+1e-30) so an empty species is not consumed\n  [info] Raf_activationBy_kRas: rate is not proportional to its reactants; divided form used with 1/(c+1e-30) so an empty species is not consumed\n  [info] Mek_activationBy_Raf: rate is not proportional to its reactants; divided form used with 1/(c+1e-30) so an empty species is not consumed\n  [info] Raf_deactivationBy_Akt: rate is not proportional to its reactants; divided form used with 1/(c+1e-30) so an empty species is not consumed\n  [info] Ras_deactivation: rate order differs from the stoichiometry; consumed on separate line(s) - \n  [info] Mek_deactivation: rate order differs from the stoichiometry; consumed on separate line(s) - \n  [info] Raf_deactivation: rate order differs from the stoichiometry; consumed on separate line(s) - \n  [info] P90_activationBy_ERK: rate is not proportional to its reactants; divided form used with 1/(c+1e-30) so an empty species is not consumed",
